In the further adventures of Oog the caveman, I was making my way
up to the Wizard when a damnfool monster with a wand of digging made
a trapdoor amongst the rubbish so I couldn't see where it was.  I
fell down it with a cockatrice corpse, but luckily I had an AoL on.
I ended up in a regular maze level.  When I got back to the entrance,
the walls were restored to their original state (I had used a wand
of digging to get in) but there was no magic portal!!

I took my levitation boots and searched around.  Found squeaky boards
but no portal.  I left the level and came back, still no portal.
So what now?  Get all the gems I can and then get killed so I can 
at least get on the scoreboard?  This is really annoying . . .
Oog is level 21, has 2 AoL's, 1 AoMB, +5 r/b Ex', the staff
(my personal Flashlight o' Conflict, left in the ON position for
when the Wizard summons his pets or does the Double Trouble thing,
that is, if I ever MEET the Wizard!), GDSM, SoR.  A pretty good
character which I hate to offer up to the great god of Q-y.

Can I get the portal back or am I screwed by another Nethack3.1
bug?


